# Core standards

- Python 3.12+. Prefer type hints and existing patterns over new abstractions.
- After code changes, run `pytest -q`. Fix failures before claiming done.
- Develop with `--model mock`. Do not assume GPU, vLLM, or CUDA.
- Do not commit or push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Read `.cursor/memory/learnings.md` and `decisions.md` before non-trivial work; append dated entries when you learn a gotcha or make an architecture decision.
- Prefer editing existing modules over adding parallel copies of logic.
- Keep README and user-facing docs free of em dashes, robotic fluff, and boasts.
